**Amendment (Released wall and reference evidence)** · `amend:decomposition:wall-reference` The paper edition {{ publication.tag }} refines (`dec:decomposition:numbers`), (`dec:decomposition:constants`), (`dec:decomposition:encoding`), (`dec:decomposition:fixtures`) and (`cor:decomposition:holds`). The reduced wall is primary and its numeraire image is the charged price; the deployment declares its fixed chartered structural floor before the first epoch (``def:epoch:safety-wall-floor``). The published controller reads the previous wall, completed width and accepted rung, applying its declared floor, deadband and cap; each epoch certifies on its own width, independently of controller performance (``def:epoch:wall-controller``, ``def:epoch:canonical-interim-wall-controller``, ``cond:epoch:safety-in-epoch-certification``). Escalation and future-width forecasts supply no certification. Bite {{ bites[1].ordinal }} retains the floor, controller and exact comparison declarations; bite {{ bites[5].ordinal }} verifies the conserved reference evidence; bite {{ bites[6].ordinal }} implements the schedules and final gates; publication and replay retain the wall, proposal, delivered charge, width, fence and verdict in the existing semantic sections. This separates economic calibration and inter-epoch tracking from the mathematical safety claim rather than leaving an obsolete calibration hold over settled rules. The independent certificate ``ver:standing:conserved-equilibrium-enclosure`` closes the shared reference-input agreement frontier, not arbitrary-input or backend evidence; the retired staged verifier supplies no conserved result. The certified scope under ``rem:dynamics:certified-bound-scope`` uses the proved fence, with no selected-path outer bound or coordinate coefficient; (`resol:design:certified-bound-scope`) records this resolution. The design records the remaining owned work in (`open:design:wall-performance`) and (`open:design:numeric-backend`). The original study rows remain historical decomposition evidence, with positional write-gate references expanded to their released labels; the current contracts are (`model:design:wall-floor`), (`alg:design:schedules`) and (`obs:design:reference-certificate`). Domain boundaries, dependencies and the eleven-bite order are unchanged.

