**Amendment (Entry admission fields)** · `amend:decomposition:entry-admission-fields` The entry rows of (`gate:design:bite-1`) under (`amend:decomposition:bite-one-entry-evidence`) declare admission_basis as review or executed, independently of claim edges. Every admission names the same accountable owner, evidence kind, status and a resolving minted admission amendment that cites its row. Review-basis rows (`gate:xchg:concept-review`), (`dec:xchg:slice-sequencing`) and (`req:interchange:fixed-once`) clear on admitted status and that evidence; they do not invent executable witnesses for review facts. Executed-basis rows (`gate:labels:implementation`) and (`gate:xchg:implementation`) additionally require current-source scoped-passed support. Submitted status never clears either basis. Either the conventional records directory or a workspace member named pn-records activates refusal while any entry is pending. The execution-coverage status and entry-admission status are separate: a review-basis row may retain held execution coverage while its reviewed entry condition is clear.

