**Amendment (Marker-bound burn settlement)** · `amend:decomposition:marker-settlement` The paper edition {{ publication.tag }} refines (`dec:decomposition:burn`), (`dec:decomposition:encoding`) and (`dec:decomposition:bites`). Burn is an amount in burn units; the numeraire converts it to reduced coordinates and is not an external price. The positive unit-cost projection states its external denomination and terms; destruction provenance supplies no normalization or universal lower bound of one, and recording-event costs remain separately published audit evidence (``cond:comparator:burn-unit-cost-projection``). An empty pre-opening acquisition interval requires a zero capacity bound with explanation; operator evidence is the applicable proved bound or an explained absence of an accruing operational role. The deployment fixes its marker policy before genesis and binds its identity and edition, recognized marker and predecessor, settled lineage, interpretation, the marker policy-selected accepted-set representation and public verification evidence into every epoch package (``post:comparator:marker-bound-settlement``, ``post:epoch:final-edge-set``). Lists or commitments with uniquely verifiable public openings must let every reader recover the complete accepted set and verify every member against the policy and both acceptance bounds. One accepted destruction snapshot and increment feed ledger, emission, width and every closure check with the writing-epoch debit vintage; authoritative act order alone does not determine this snapshot. Bite 2 introduces and validates amount, cost, marker-policy, lineage and accepted-set carriers in pn-records, with host recognition evidence and cases; bite 5 derives the snapshot and first-accepted increments in pn-epoch for the ledger; bite 7 checks common-marker closure; bite 8 publishes and persists the complete evidence; bite 9 reconstructs it offline. The original study rows remain historical planning evidence, with removed paper aliases moved to their released successors; these obligations refine their burn and package content without changing domain boundaries, dependencies or bite order. Conditional consistency is settled, while concrete realization evidence, open placement and cadence remain deployment obligations without a promise of compulsory or timed acceptance (`rule:design:marker-recognition`), (`alg:design:burn-snapshot`).

**Amendment (Dimensional comparison scope)** · `amend:decomposition:dimensional-scope` The paper edition {{ publication.tag }} refines the numeric and fixture contracts of (`dec:decomposition:numbers`) and (`dec:decomposition:fixtures`). Fixed purchasing power under a market price increase by a factor requires the numeric burn amount divided by that factor; unit recoinage instead co-expresses the numeraire and burn amounts (``subsec:necessity:floor-as-numeraire``). External unit cost multiplies burn-unit quantities, including numeraire-converted action charges, never unconverted action quantities (``cond:comparator:burn-unit-cost-projection``, ``eq:comparator:admission-benchmark-deposits``). The width scaling and fence-certificate degradation in ``prop:epoch:compensation`` both assume the declared comparison-family law; neither follows from the invariant door-price product. Bite {{ bites[1].ordinal }} tests these distinctions before burn carriers can support ledger or economic claims (`inv:design:units`), (`verif:design:numerical-boundaries`).
